"kind":"trace",
"id":"compress_events",
"source":"compress_events.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    pos = 0\n    n = int(data[pos])\n    pos += 1\n    days = []\n    types = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        day = int(data[pos])\n        pos += 1\n        event_type = int(data[pos])\n        pos += 1\n        days.append(day)\n        types.append(event_type)\n\n    uniq = sorted(set(days))\n    rank = {}\n    for i, day in enumerate(uniq):\n        rank[day] = i\n\n    seen = []\n    for day in uniq:\n        seen.append(set())\n    for k in range(n):\n        d = days[k]\n        t = types[k]\n        r = rank[d]\n        seen[r].add(t)\n\n    counts = [len(s) for s in seen]\n    print(\"\\n\".join(map(str, counts)))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program reads every reading first, sorts the distinct days into a small compressed range, then files each reading's event type into a set indexed by its day's compressed rank, so a count of distinct event types per day never needs an array sized to the full day range.",
"presets":[
